      "figure": "arith-vs-geo",
      "body": "Once you know the type, use its rule: arithmetic a_n = a_1 + (n − 1)d, geometric a_n = a_1 · r^(n−1). First classify the sequence, then apply the matching formula."
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "First name the pattern, then run it.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "sequenceBuild",
        "prompt": "It's arithmetic. Dial d so the 5th term of 2, 5, 8, 11, … lands on 14.",
        "mode": "arithmetic",
        "first": 2,
        "targetD": 3,
        "atPosition": 5,
        "targetTerm": 14,
        "successFeedback": "d = 3: four gaps — 2 + 4·3 = 14. Naming the pattern type is what unlocked the formula.",
        "lowFeedback": "Too small — position 5 lands short of 14.",
        "highFeedback": "Too big — position 5 overshoots 14. One gap in 2, 5, 8 settles it."
      },
      "predict": {
        "prompt": "2, 5, 8, 11, … — is the same amount ADDED each step, or MULTIPLIED?",
