        "outcomeId": "add",
        "reveal": "2 → 5 could be +3 or ×2.5 — but 5 → 8 is +3 and NOT ×2.5 (that would be 12.5). Adding wins: arithmetic, so the linear formula applies. The second gap is always the tiebreaker."
      },
      "conceptTag": "fn-choose-formula",
